##### FFBSS

Food Excluding Food and Beverage Serving Services (FFBSS) carries a weight of 651 within the CPI basket. Although it has a smaller weight than Food and Beverage Serving Services (FBSS), it includes items related to grocery consumption, which affect the daily spending of most households.

The FFBSS subgroup is further divided into **10** detailed classes, including - Rice and Cereals (122), - Meat (101), - Fish and Seafood (79), - Milk, Other Dairy Products and Eggs (64), - Oils and Fats (12), - Fruits and Nuts (79), - Vegetables (82), - Sugar, Confectionery and Desserts (27), - Ready Made and Other Food Products (44), - and Non Alcoholic Beverages (41).

```{r}
